cing is transmitted by grafting from silenced stocks to non-silenced scions.</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>4738</fpage><lpage>4745</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9303318</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000038-Himber1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Himber</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Dunoyer</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Moissiard</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Ritzenthaler</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Voinnet</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Transitivity-dependent and -independent cell-to-cell movement of RNA silencing.</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><volume>22</volume><fpage>4523</fpage><lpage>4533</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12941703</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000038-Palauqui2"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Palauqui</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaucheret</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Transgenes are dispensable for the RNA degradation step of cosuppression.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>9675</fpage><lpage>9680</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9689140</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000038-GarciaPerez1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garcia-Perez</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Houdt</surname><given-names>HV</given-names></name><name><surname>Depicker</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Spreading of post-transcriptional gene silencing along the target gene promotes sy